WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.275
Lesson 9.3.

00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:04.150
Building a combined system.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.230
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.372
be able to design a portfolio that

00:00:08.372 --> 00:00:10.941
uses exchange grid bots and DeFi together

00:00:10.941 --> 00:00:13.205
without doubling up on the same risk.

00:00:14.505 --> 00:00:15.795
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.795 --> 00:00:17.480
First, the key ideas.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.195
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:20.195 --> 00:00:21.720
Then, your checklist.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.882
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:25.182 --> 00:00:26.597
Each tool is good at a

00:00:26.597 --> 00:00:29.172
different job: The trap: correlation.

00:00:29.172 --> 00:00:32.883
An ETH grid bot + an ETH/USDC

00:00:32.883 --> 00:00:36.223
LP + an LST loop are three

00:00:36.223 --> 00:00:40.357
bets on ETH staying in a range.

00:00:40.357 --> 00:00:43.542
If ETH breaks down, they all lose together.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:46.456
Add up your exposure by underlying asset and

00:00:46.456 --> 00:00:49.152
by range, not by number of positions.

00:00:49.152 --> 00:00:51.795
First, Grid bots → capture oscillation

00:00:51.795 --> 00:00:55.077
in range-bound major pairs, fully automated.

00:00:55.077 --> 00:00:57.797
Next, DeFi lending / stable LP →

00:00:57.797 --> 00:01:01.229
earn on idle stablecoins and reserves.

00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:03.716
Then, Staking / LSTs → earn

00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:06.504
on assets you'd hold anyway.

00:01:06.504 --> 00:01:09.658
And finally, Concentrated LP → earn fees

00:01:09.658 --> 00:01:13.734
on-chain in ranges, for larger, self-custodied sizes.

00:01:15.034 --> 00:01:19.059
Percentages are an example structure, not a recommendation.

00:01:19.059 --> 00:01:21.109
Set your own from your risk budget.

00:01:21.109 --> 00:01:24.737
Rules for this system: Reserve, 15%, Stablecoin

00:01:24.737 --> 00:01:28.440
lending (split across 2 protocols), Liquidity to

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.444
defend positions and redeploy after range breaks.

00:01:32.444 --> 00:01:35.655
Core yield, 25%, Stable-stable LP /

00:01:35.655 --> 00:01:39.165
stable lending, Base return on cash.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:42.652
Hold-anyway assets, 25%, Staking /

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:46.240
LSTs, Earn on long-term holdings.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.133
Range income, 30%, Grid bots on liquid majors

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:54.750
(+ optional wide on-chain LP), Capture oscillation.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:01.209
Speculative, ≤5%, Burner-wallet farms, airdrops, new protocols, Capped experiments.

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:03.969
Here's your checklist.

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:05.504
Do it now, for real.

00:02:05.504 --> 00:02:08.464
First, Exposure added up by underlying

00:02:08.464 --> 00:02:11.269
asset, not by bot/position count.

00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:14.444
Next, Reserve sized and kept out of positions.

00:02:14.444 --> 00:02:16.679
Then, Profit sweep schedule set.

00:02:16.679 --> 00:02:20.370
And finally, one journal covering bots and DeFi positions.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:22.880
Question 1.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.223
ETH grid bot + ETH/USDC

00:02:27.223 --> 00:02:30.780
LP + ETH LST loop.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.365
How many independent bets?

00:02:36.785 --> 00:02:39.172
The answer: Essentially one: ETH

00:02:39.172 --> 00:02:41.425
staying in range or rising.

00:02:41.425 --> 00:02:42.445
They're correlated.

00:02:43.745 --> 00:02:44.990
Question 2.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:46.265
What is the reserve for?

00:02:50.685 --> 00:02:53.204
The answer: Defending debt positions and

00:02:53.204 --> 00:02:56.645
redeploying after invalidations, without forced selling.

00:02:57.945 --> 00:02:59.215
Question 3.

00:02:59.215 --> 00:03:01.120
Why sweep profits out of positions?

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.428
The answer: Profits left in a

00:03:07.428 --> 00:03:09.930
position stay exposed to its risks.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.300
Sweeping locks them in.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.845
Let's recap.

00:03:13.845 --> 00:03:16.180
Grid bots → capture oscillation in

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.215
range-bound major pairs, fully automated.

00:03:19.215 --> 00:03:21.491
DeFi lending / stable LP →

00:03:21.491 --> 00:03:24.995
earn on idle stablecoins and reserves.

00:03:24.995 --> 00:03:26.922
Staking / LSTs → earn

00:03:26.922 --> 00:03:29.675
on assets you'd hold anyway.

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:32.626
Concentrated LP → earn fees on-chain

00:03:32.626 --> 00:03:36.135
in ranges, for larger, self-custodied sizes.

00:03:37.435 --> 00:03:39.950
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.125
Next up, Lesson 10.0: Mastery Starter.
